{
  "answer": "When FastAPI runs behind a proxy that adds a path prefix, you should configure it using the `root_path` parameter. This allows you to declare a path in your code, such as `/app`, and have the proxy add a path prefix like `/api/v1` to the request. FastAPI will then handle the request as if it was served at the declared path, `/app`, without requiring changes to your application code. This is useful for scenarios where you have a proxy layer that modifies the request path. [advanced/behind-a-proxy-6]",
